:"step.unique_valuation","kind":"claim","label":"The unique-valuation step","locator":"Appendix B, after Theorem B.1, p. 16","source_id":"paper.short.pdf","statement":"Fix a divisibility-maximal $n\\in F$ with $n\\ge2$ and a prime $\\ell\\mid\\Phi_n(b)$. Every other selected exponent $m$ satisfies $n\\nmid m$, hence $v_\\ell(b^m-1)<e$, so the $n$th summand has the uniquely smallest $\\ell$-adic valuation and cannot cancel. Thus $\\ell^e\\mid D_F$ and $n\\mid\\operatorname{ord}_{D_F}(b)$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/step.unique_valuation","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/short.res-period","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22short.res-period%22%2C%22step.unique_valuation%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22short.res-period%22%2C%22step.unique_valuation%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/step.unique_valuation"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/step.unique_valuation","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22step.unique_valuation%22%2C%22step.cyclotomic_prime_power%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22step.unique_valuation%22%2C%22step.cyclotomic_prime_power%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/step.cyclotomic_prime_power"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":